  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "You'll now fix the ramp by adding a collider component, which is essential for physical interactions in Unity. A collider is a component that defines the shape of an object for the purpose of physical collisions and interactions within the environment. Without a collider, an object has no physical boundaries and other objects can go right through it \u2014 like a cloud.\n\nThe sphere primitive you added earlier for the ball already came with a <b>Sphere</b> collider \u2014 that's what the Physics Material is attached to.\n\nUnity provides various collider shapes (such as sphere, cube, and capsule colliders). However, since the ramp has an irregular shape, you\u2019ll use something called a <b>Mesh</b> collider, which conforms to the unique shape of the object\u2019s mesh (3D shape)."
